#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Run the workspace checks against an identified, unchanged source snapshot.

Independent checks (host tests, analysis, sharded Dart tests) run concurrently.
Dart test files are split into balanced shards, one `flutter test` process each.
Theme-parametrized Dart tests run the default theme plus one sampled variant per
file; `--all-themes` (or RAFT_TEST_ALL_THEMES=1) runs the full theme matrix.
A failing or timed-out test is listed in `.local/check-summary.txt`. Knobs:
RAFT_CHECK_SHARDS, RAFT_CHECK_JOBS (flutter test `-j` per shard),
RAFT_CHECK_SHARD_TIMEOUT_MINUTES (whole-shard watchdog).

Flaky tests do not force a whole re-run. When the ONLY failing checks are Dart test
shards (analysis, lints, the structure audit, host tests and pub get are never
retried), the failed test files plus files that never finished are re-run alone with
`flutter test <file>`, up to RAFT_CHECK_RETRIES attempts each (default 3, 0 = no
retry), stopping at the first pass. A file that passes on a retry is a flake: the
run may pass, and the final JSON lists it as
"flaky": [{"file", "tests": [failed test names of the first run], "errors": [their first-run failure messages], "attempts": n}]
(n = retry attempts used) while the summary prints "FLAKY (passed on retry)". A
file that fails every attempt keeps the run failed. More than 6 files to retry
(real breakage), an early stop (max failures, compile error, stall, failed static check) or a failure
without a test file means no retry at all.

An identical code tree is not checked twice. A full pass on a clean worktree
(`git status --porcelain` empty) is recorded under
${RAFT_CHECK_CACHE:-~/.cache/raft-check}/passed/<tree>.json, keyed by
`git rev-parse HEAD^{tree}` (with time, HEAD commit and the final JSON; a pass with
flakes is recorded too). `--reuse` prints "tree <hash> already passed ..." plus the
stored JSON with "reused": true and exits 0 without running anything, when the
worktree is clean and that tree has a recorded pass (an `--all-themes` run only
reuses an all-themes pass). A dirty worktree never reuses and runs normally.

The gate fails fast so a broken branch does not hold the shared lock for a full
run: the shards' output is watched while they run, and every process this run
started is killed on the first compile/load error, once RAFT_CHECK_MAX_FAILURES
tests have failed (default 3, 0 = never stop early), or when no shard printed
anything for RAFT_CHECK_STALL_MINUTES (default 10, 0 = off). Each step is appended
to /tmp/raft-flutter-gate-events.log (tool/gate_events.py), with a terminal
PASS/FAIL/ERROR line on every path; RAFT_GATE_NOTIFY_TARGET also sends failures.

Usage: tool/check-project [--all-themes] [--reuse]
"""
